## PIN lines for Green (the file header holds the same text)

- `line-art-fix.ts` exports `StorytimeLineArtFixEntry`, `StorytimeLineArtFixTable`, `readStorytimeLineArtFixTable()`, `applyStorytimeLineArtFixes(files, kind, table?)`, `fillStorytimeLineArtHair(gray, fill)`.
- An entry holds `sourceFile`, `sourceSha256`, `replacement` (relative to `content/storytime/`), `replacementSha256`, `reason`, and for D7 `fill` with `seed`, `areaPx`, `bbox`.
- A `line` file swaps only when its bytes hold `sourceSha256`; it keeps `fileName`. A `color` file and an unlisted row do not change. A wrong or missing replacement throws `line-art fix: ...`.
- The fill throws `line-art fill: ...` for a seed on ink, a region that touches the border, a wrong area, and a wrong box. A right region becomes black and the source stays equal.
- The filled files are `l2/print/pictures-fix/<source without -line-v1.png>-hair-v1.png`.
- The two nose rows only carry `data-edge-ink="clip"`, with one rule `.picture-box[data-edge-ink] img { clip-path: inset(1.5mm); }`.
- The printed border width is `max(1, floor(cssMm * 96 / 25.4)) * 25.4 / 96` mm.
- X5 pins `.match-choices` as the only dotted rule and the three dashed selectors `.map-place`, `.perforation`, `.fold-line`. This keeps the dashed set exact and non-vacuous; `.match-choices` is a match line, not a frame.

